  loadSkills(7,['Distinguish population, sample, parameter and statistic','Define a sampling distribution','Explain sample-to-sample variability','Enumerate exact samples for a tiny population','Construct an exact sampling distribution','Explain E(X̄)=μ and unbiasedness','Define standard error','Use σX̄=σ/√n','Explain why larger n reduces SE','Identify one observation X','Identify a sample mean X̄','Choose the centre for X̄','Choose the spread for X̄','Interpret a sample-mean probability in context','Recognise normal population with known σ','State the centre, variance and SE of X̄','Solve a left-tail mean probability','Solve a between mean probability','Solve a right-tail mean probability','Solve an inverse mean boundary','Find central symmetric limits for sample means','State what becomes approximately normal under CLT','Recognise exact normality from a normal population','Recognise large-enough-n CLT logic','Apply CLT to a mean from an exponential population','Retain the original mean and SE under CLT','Recognise σ known versus σ unknown','Replace σ with sample s when σ is unknown','Recognise the Student-t sampling model','Calculate T for a sample mean','Determine df=n−1','Obtain cumulative t probability in Excel','Discriminate the Z case from the t case','Identify p=X/n','Identify population parameter π','Check proportion approximation conditions > 5','Use centre π','Use theoretical SE when π is known','Use observed p for estimated SE when requested','Solve a sample-proportion probability','Solve central limits for p','Interpret a probability about p','Explain how n changes the p distribution','Recognise two independent sample means','Choose centre μ₁−μ₂','Choose SE √(σ₁²/n₁+σ₂²/n₂)','Translate wording into a difference event','Solve a two-mean probability','Preserve group order','Interpret a difference probability','Check independence and model conditions','Recognise finite-population sampling without replacement','Calculate sampling fraction n/N','Decide whether FPC is needed','Use FPC √[(N−n)/(N−1)]','Apply FPC to mean SE','Explain why FPC reduces SE'],52);
